<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.3.1: Solving Equations with Fractions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02361</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.3.1: Solving Equations with Fractions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6059c61c-eea4-457c-866c-f47bb58b91c8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up (5 minutes) </title>
<para>The purpose of this Math Talk is to elicit strategies and understandings students have for operations on fractions
  and solving equations. These understandings help students develop fluency and will be helpful later in this lesson
  when students will need to use similar computations to solve quadratic equations.</para>
<title>Launch</title>
<para>Display one problem at a time. Give students quiet time to think individually for each problem and ask them to give a
  signal when they have an answer and a strategy. Keep all problems displayed throughout the talk. Follow with a
  whole-class discussion.</para>

<div class="os-raise-extrasupport">
  <note>
    <para>Support for English Language Learners<title>Support for English Language Learners</title></para>
    <para>MLR 8 Discussion Supports: Speaking<title>MLR 8 Discussion Supports: Speaking</title></para>
  </note>
  <div class="os-raise-extrasupport-body">
    <para>Display sentence frames to support students when they explain their strategy. For example, "First, I _____ because . . ." or "I noticed _____ so I . . . ." Some students may benefit from the opportunity to rehearse what they will say with a partner before they share with the whole class.</para>
    <para class="os-raise-text-italicize">Design Principle(s): Optimize output (for explanation)</para>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="os-raise-extrasupport">
  <note>
    <para>Support for Students with Disabilities<title>Support for Students with Disabilities</title></para>
    <para>Representation: Internalize Comprehension<title>Representation: Internalize Comprehension</title></para>
   </note>
  <div class="os-raise-extrasupport-body">
    <para>To support working memory, provide students with sticky notes or mini whiteboards.</para>
    <para class="os-raise-text-italicize">Supports accessibility for: Memory; Organization</para>
  </div></div>


<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>Solve each equation mentally.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x+x=\frac14\)</item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=\frac18\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((\frac{3}{2})^2=x\)</item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=\frac94\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(\frac{3}{5}+x=\frac95\)</item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=\frac65\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(\frac{1}{12}+x=\frac14\)</item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answer in simplest form, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=\frac16\)</para>
<title>Activity Synthesis</title>
<para>Ask students to share their strategies for each problem. Record and display their responses for all to see. To
  involve more students in the conversation, consider asking:</para>
<list>
  <item> "Who can restate __________'s reasoning in a different way?" </item>
  <item> "Did anyone have the same strategy but would explain it differently?" </item>
  <item> "Did anyone solve the problem in a different way?" </item>
  <item> "Does anyone want to add on to __________'s strategy?" </item>
  <item> "Do you agree or disagree? Why?" </item>
</list></section>
